{# Charmed OpenSearch release notes template.

   Reproduces the structure of the product's published release notes, most
   recently revision 315:
   https://canonical.com/data/opensearch/docs/2/reference/release-notes/revision-315/
   source: canonical/opensearch-operator,
           docs/reference/release-notes/revision-315.md

   Differences from base.md.j2, and why:
   - MyST frontmatter with `html_meta.description` and a
     `(reference-release-notes-revision-N)=` anchor, as the docs build requires.
     The frontmatter must end up on line 1 of the saved file: if a review-notes
     HTML comment is added, it goes AFTER the frontmatter block. Otherwise
     Sphinx parses the `---` fences as body transitions and warns
     "Document headings start at H2, not H1".
   - Title is `# Revision N` (the docs site supplies the product name), and the
     date line is plain text ("December 16, 2025"), not bold as in the base.
   - Intro links use Diataxis cross-references (`how-to-deploy-standard`,
     `how-to-minor-upgrade`, `reference-system-requirements`) resolved by the
     docs build, not absolute URLs.
   - Category headings render at `###`, not `##`, because this product groups
     changes under a per-component `## <Component name>` heading first (e.g.
     `## Charmed OpenSearch`, `## Charmed OpenSearch Dashboards`). The builder
     handles one repository per run, so it emits the `###` category headings
     only — the merge/polish pass adds the `## <Component name>` heading above
     each component's block. Section names themselves match DA186 exactly
     (Features / Bug fixes / Other improvements), so no renaming is needed.
   - Entries use `* ` bullets, wrap Jira IDs in square brackets, and link the
     PR as `([PR \#N](url))` with an escaped `#` — no commit link:
     `* [[DPE-1234](url)] message ([PR \#612](url))`
   - Compatibility is a per-charm table with an OpenSearch version column, a
     "Minimum Juju version" column and an Artifacts (snap) column; revisions
     link to a `tree/revNNN` tag, not to a release page.
#}
{% extends "base.md.j2" %}

{% block frontmatter %}
---
myst:
  html_meta:
    description: "Charmed OpenSearch {{ title }} release notes - TODO: one-sentence summary of the headline changes."
---

(reference-release-notes-{{ title | lower | replace(" ", "-") }})=
{% endblock %}

{% block date_line %}

{{ date }}
{% endblock %}

{% block introduction %}

<!-- TODO: Write a brief summary of the most important changes in this release. -->

{% block intro_links %}
[Charmhub](https://charmhub.io/opensearch) | [Deploy guide](how-to-deploy-standard) | [Upgrade instructions](how-to-minor-upgrade) | [System requirements](reference-system-requirements)
{% endblock %}
{% endblock %}

{% block changelog %}
{% for category in category_order %}
{% if categories.get(category) %}

### {{ category }}

{% for entry in categories[category] %}
* {% if entry.jira_ids %}{% for jira in entry.jira_ids %}[[{{ jira }}](https://warthogs.atlassian.net/browse/{{ jira }})]{% endfor %} {% endif %}{{ entry.message }}{% if entry.pr_number %} ([PR \#{{ entry.pr_number }}]({{ entry.pr_url }})){% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}

{% block compatibility %}
| Charm | Revision | Hardware architecture | OpenSearch version | Minimum Juju version | Artifacts |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Charmed OpenSearch | TODO | AMD64 | TODO | 3.5+ | Snap: TODO |
| Charmed OpenSearch Dashboards | TODO | AMD64 | TODO | 3.5+ | Snap: TODO |
{% endblock %}
